---
permalink: /tools/
title: Tools — Free and open-source macOS apps
description: Small, free and open-source macOS menu bar apps — Quay, a control center for your local dev stack, and LeanBattery, an 11-point-wide battery indicator.
keywords: macos apps, open source, menu bar apps, developer tools, quay, leanbattery
generate_social_image: false
breadcrumb: tools
---

{% extends "./_layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block custom_style %}
	{% set css_tools %}{% include "css/tools.css" %}{% endset %}
	{{ css_tools | cssmin | safe }}
{% endblock %}

{# ponytail: inline list, one object per app. Move to _data/tools.yaml if it outgrows ~5 entries. #}
{% set tools = [
	{
		name: "Quay",
		url: "/quay/",
		logo: "/assets/img/quay/logo.svg",
		logoWidth: 64,
		logoHeight: 64,
		tagline: "Your entire local dev stack. One menu bar.",
		blurb: "Start, stop and monitor dev servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and AI coding agents — with live health, CPU and memory, and port-conflict detection.",
		badges: ["macOS", "Universal", "Tauri v2", "MIT"]
	},
	{
		name: "LeanBattery",
		url: "/lean-battery/",
		logo: "/assets/img/lean-battery/menubar-discharging.png",
		logoWidth: 32,
		logoHeight: 64,
		tagline: "A battery indicator that doesn't hog your menubar.",
		blurb: "Battery level and charging state in an 11-point-wide upright battery — with per-app energy use, battery health and low-battery alerts you set yourself.",
		badges: ["macOS", "Apple Silicon", "Swift 6", "MIT"]
	}
] %}

{% block main %}
	<section class="block tools-head">
		<h1>Tools</h1>
		<p>Small, free and open-source apps I build for macOS. No accounts, no telemetry — just download and run.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="block tools-list">
		<ul class="tools-grid">
			{% for tool in tools %}
			<li>
				<a class="nostyle tool-card" href="{{ tool.url }}">
					<div class="tool-logo"><img src="{{ tool.logo }}" alt="" width="{{ tool.logoWidth }}" height="{{ tool.logoHeight }}" /></div>
					<h2>{{ tool.name }}</h2>
					<p class="tool-tagline">{{ tool.tagline }}</p>
					<p class="tool-blurb">{{ tool.blurb }}</p>
					<ul class="tool-badges">
						{% for badge in tool.badges %}<li>{{ badge }}</li>{% endfor %}
					</ul>
					<span class="tool-more">Learn more <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
				</a>
			</li>
			{% endfor %}
		</ul>
	</section>
{% endblock %}
